{"caption":"ReasoningBank memory retrieval, extraction, and consolidation process","description":"A process diagram shows a memory bank, a task timeline, and how past experiences are used to create and store memory items. At the top left, a rounded box labeled “ReasoningBank: a collection of memory items” represents the bank. A downward arrow labeled “(i) Memory Retrieval” leads from it to an “ℋ: experience/trajectory” box. Inside that box, a person/task symbol marked qᵢ points to an Agent robot, which has a two-way connection with an Env screen icon. The trajectory then points right to “LLM-as-a-Judge.” The judge branches to “Success Insights,” marked with a green check, and “Failure Reflection,” marked with a red cross. An arrow points right from these assessment outcomes toward an icon labeled “Memory Items.” From the memory items, an upward arrow labeled “(iii) Memory Consolidation” leads back to ReasoningBank. The extraction stage is labeled “(ii) Memory Extraction.”

On the right, a rounded example panel shows a memory item at the top, with a clipboard icon, the label “Memory Item j,” and fields separated from it by a dotted vertical divider: “Title: Prioritize user account sections for personal data”; “Description When a query requests user-specific ...”; and “Content: Systematically look for and click on links ...”. Below is a “Memory Extractor” label with an icon. An upward arrow rises from the example trajectory/task area toward the memory-item area. The “Experience/Trajectory ℋ” row contains the excerpt “<think>... I need to navigate to ...</think>” and “<action> click('188') </action>”. The “Task qᵢ” row reads “Tell me the status of my latest order and when it will arrive.”

A horizontal timeline runs beneath the process and ends in a right-pointing arrow labeled “Time.” It marks “Task q₁,” “Task q₂,” an ellipsis, a highlighted “Task qᵢ,” another ellipsis, and “Task qₙ,” indicating tasks arriving over time.","figure_type":"diagram","chart_values":[]}
